n":"1788540043006738260-df00a118-8f47-4fd6-ae23-dcea8acc1c5a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete in fresh worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/docs-orphan-process-runbook` from `origin/main@5932f4951b27`.\n\n- Replaced the 80-line background-helper section in `AGENTS.md` with a 21-line prevention contract.\n- Preserved the wall-clock bounded spawn, process-group trap, subagent cleanup duty, no-PPID-1 invariant, unbounded-busy-loop prohibition, fixed-end preference, and bounded-gate timeout exception.\n- Added `docs/orphaned-processes.md` with the dated incident evidence, prevention rationale, read-only detector and interpretation, and confirmed operator reclamation sequence.\n- Indexed the page under Operations in `docs/README.md`.\n- Defined the section budget verification as physical source lines from its H2 heading through the line before the next H2.\n\nVerification:\n- `python scripts/check_docs_index.py`: PASS.\n- `pytest -q tests/unit/test_check_docs_index.py`: 20 passed.\n- `make lint` with the worktree virtualenv and pinned uv first on PATH: PASS.\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\n\nNext: commit with DCO, Change-Id, and the full rebar ticket trailer, then push to Gerrit for both required votes.","timestamp":1788539655797934185}],"created_at":1788538518827650442,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d88881e9-b38b-4a46-924a-3d71daf1c6c0","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3960-1016-ad4b-4c90"},{"link_uuid":"df00a118-8f47-4fd6-ae23-dcea8acc1c5a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c0d0-07b1-c699-4908"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`AGENTS.md` says launch-loaded guidance must stay lean and point to maintained documentation (`AGENTS.md:10-15`), but its background-process section embeds a dated incident narrative, operator recovery procedure, and detector explanation across lines 252-330. Every agent pays that context cost even when it only needs the prevention contract.\n\n## Approach\n- Replace the long `AGENTS.md` section with a compact, imperative prevention contract that retains the safety invariants, spawn-time bound and process-group cleanup example, explicit exemption for bounded LLM gate operations, and a pointer to detailed documentation.\n- Move the incident evidence, detector usage, false-positive interpretation, and operator recovery procedure into a new maintained operations page at `docs/orphaned-processes.md`.\n- Add the new page to the Operations section of `docs/README.md`.\n- Preserve commands and facts needed to prevent, detect, and reclaim orphaned processes. Do not copy unrelated tracker or implementation history.\n\n## Scope\n- `AGENTS.md`: compress the launch-loaded background-process rule.\n- `docs/orphaned-processes.md`: own the detailed incident evidence, prevention rationale, detector interpretation, and operator recovery steps.\n- `docs/README.md`: index the new operations page.\n\n## Testing\n- Run `python scripts/check_docs_index.py`.\n- Run the repository documentation checks and `make lint` with the worktree virtualenv first on PATH.\n- Inspect the rendered Markdown structure and verify every moved command and safety invariant remains reachable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The `AGENTS.md` background-process section contains no more than 35 logical lines.\n- [ ] The compact section includes a wall-clock-bounded spawn plus process-group cleanup example.\n- [ ] The compact section states that no spawned process may reach PPID 1 and that each subagent must reap its own helpers.\n- [ ] The compact section prohibits unbounded busy loops without a wall-clock bound.\n- [ ] The compact section explicitly forbids applying timeouts to bounded LLM gate operations.\n- [ ] Dated incident evidence is absent from `AGENTS.md` and present in `docs/orphaned-processes.md`.\n- [ ] Orphan-detector interpretation and operator reclamation steps are absent from `AGENTS.md` and present in `docs/orphaned-processes.md`.\n- [ ] The Operations section of `docs/README.md` links `orphaned-processes.md` and describes it as the prevention, detection, and recovery procedure for orphaned processes.\n- [ ] The detailed page documents the bounded-spawn, process-group-cleanup, read-only-detection, and confirmed-reclamation commands.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_docs_index.py` passes.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes with the worktree virtualenv first on PATH.\n- [ ] Gerrit reports `LLM-Review +1`.\n- [ ] Gerrit reports `Verified +1`.\n- [ ] Gerrit reports no unresolved comments.\n- [ ] The change is submitted to `main`.\n\n## Verification\nCompare the pre-change and post-change section line counts, search both files for each preserved invariant and command, run the documentation index/link checker, run `make lint`, then confirm Gerrit labels and merged status before closing the ticket.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"Replace the launch-loaded orphan-process narrative with a concise prevention contract and documentation pointer."},{"path":"docs/orphaned-processes.md","reason":"Own detailed incident evidence, prevention rationale, detector interpretation, and operator recovery steps."},{"path":"docs/README.md","reason":"Index the new operations page for discovery."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","c0d0-07b1-c699-4908"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7b562c96-9211-4311